n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]machine:X shows exactly the nodes machine X's own TUI shows — same [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]count, grouping, statuses, and chips — with stale owner-side rows [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]retired and `sase screenshot` able to drive query filters [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]unattended for the cross-machine evidence captures.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202609/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]remote_dispatch_agents_tab_parity.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202609/remote_dispatch_agents_tab_parity.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-133[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-133/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Owner served-set parity[/bold #D7AFFF]                                       [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]owner-served-set-parity[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]owner-served-set-parity: make the gateway snapshot serve exactly the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rows the owner's own TUI presents — retire dead-PID protected waiting [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rows, honor owner dismissal state, and harden liveness beyond bare [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]kill(pid,0) — with the selection decision unit-tested in sase_core.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Wire presentation facts[/bold #D7AFFF]                                       [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]wire-presentation-facts[dim] · [dim][/dim]after owner-served-set-parity[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]wire-presentation-facts: extend the fleet contract additively so every [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]row carries the owner-presented display status, family/parent linkage [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]for historical shells, resolved tribe/clan tribe, and both runtime [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]timestamps, populated by the gateway projection and covered by golden [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]wire fixtures.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Viewer remote-node render parity[/bold #D7AFFF]                              [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]viewer-remote-node-parity[dim] · [dim][/dim]after wire-presentation-facts[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]viewer-remote-node-parity: render remote rows through the same grouping [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and presentation paths as local rows — tribe panels, nested done shells,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]shell-count and proc/gate/monitor chips, owner status text, and banner [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]counts that include done nodes — differing only by the machine chip.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase screenshot text-input driving[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]screenshot-text-input[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]screenshot-text-input: add an ordered, repeatable --type option that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sends literal text interleaved with -p presses and -w waits, forward it [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]through the remote --host leg, and cover ordering and remote argv [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]forwarding with tests, so query filters can be driven unattended.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-133","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-133.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","role_suffix":"plan","vcs_provider":"GitHub","workflow_name":"sase-133.1"},"source_run_id":"run-67719c219bd8c5abe0b13ce95819150e","started_at":"2026-09-18T21:00:42.732356+00:00",